## What a `type: engine` instance is

**An engine memorial describes a first-class rule body evaluation engine** — the substrate that compiles and executes rule bodies.  Engines are typed-edge graph citizens — declarative, queryable, introspectable — not just `engine:` field discriminator values.

Rules reference engines via `uses-engine:` typed-edge:

```yaml
type: rule
uses-engine:
  - engines/clara-rules.md
```

Engine is a subtype of [`meta`](meta.md) — memorials about the memory system itself.

## Canonical engines

Common engines that may be loaded as instances:

- **`engines/plain-pattern.md`** — simple structural match (ELIZA-like)
- **`engines/malli.md`** — schema-validated rule bodies (Malli library)
- **`engines/clara-rules.md`** — production-rule forward-chaining (Rete + TMS)
- **`engines/core-logic.md`** — relational / bidirectional inference (miniKanren substrate)
- **`engines/meander-strategy.md`** — term-rewriting strategy composition (Stratego tradition)

Each engine has its own memorial declaring rule-body-shape, dispatch-strategy-default, complexity-tier, performance-characteristics, and library-implementation.

