## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Engine memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` plus type-specific required slots:

- **`rule-body-shape`** (required) — `plain-pattern` / `malli-schema` / `clara-data-form` / `core-logic-goal` / `meander-strategy` / `datalog-query` / etc.
- **`dispatch-strategy-default`** — `:graph-query` / `:match-compile`
- **`complexity-tier`** — `simple` / `moderate` / `complex`
- **`performance-characteristics`** — Big-O / lookup characteristics
- **`library-implementation`** — typed-edge to underlying library
- **`applicable-rule-body-classes`** — what kinds of rule bodies use this engine

{{slot-table}}

## Canonical body structure

```markdown
## What this engine evaluates

<Semantic shape of the rule bodies this engine handles.>

## When to use

<Trigger conditions favoring this engine over alternatives.>

## When NOT to use

<Counter-conditions where another engine is a better fit.>

## Performance characteristics

<Complexity / scale envelope; hot-path suitability; memory profile.>

## Library implementation

<Cross-reference to the library memorial.  Pin version where it
matters.>

## Example rule bodies

<2-3 illustrative rule memorials using this engine.>

## See also

<Adjacent engines, rules using this engine, library memorial.>
```

## What an engine memorial is NOT

- **Not a library** — the engine reference's `library-implementation:` typed-edge points to the underlying library; the engine memorial is the SUBSTRATE-DESIGN summary
- **Not a rule** — engines evaluate rule bodies; engines themselves don't fire
- **Not a discriminator value** — engines are FIRST-CLASS memorials, not field values

